# UI Copy via AppStrings

All user-facing text (labels, titles, buttons, placeholders, alerts, empty states) must come from `PsychologyApp.Presentation.Common.AppStrings`.

Do not hardcode UI strings in ViewModels, pages, or XAML bindings when the copy is shown to users.

## Rules

- Bind / assign UI text from `AppStrings` properties or methods
- Add missing strings to `AppStrings.cs` using `T(russian, english)`
- Prefer descriptive PascalCase names (`JournalNotePlaceholder`, `PracticeGoHomeButton`)
- Parameterized copy uses methods: `AppStrings.ProfileStreakCount(days)`
- Non-UI strings (logs, exception messages for developers, keys, IDs) may stay inline

## Examples

```csharp
// ❌ BAD
Title = "Дневник";
NotePlaceholder = "Write a note…";

// ✅ GOOD
Title = AppStrings.JournalTitle;
NotePlaceholder = AppStrings.JournalNotePlaceholder;
```

```csharp
// ❌ BAD — new copy invented in the ViewModel
public string SaveLabel => "Сохранить";

// ✅ GOOD — add to AppStrings, then use
// AppStrings.cs:
public static string SaveButton => T("Сохранить", "Save");
// ViewModel:
public string SaveLabel => AppStrings.SaveButton;
```
